    "title_en": "Measurements of the branching fractions of \\boldmath $χ_{cJ}\\toΣ^0\\barΣ^0η$",
    "abstract_en": "Using $(2712.4\\pm14.3)\\times10^{6}$$ψ(3686)$ events collected with the BESIII detector at the BEPCII collider, we report the first observations of the decay $χ_{cJ}(J=0,1,2) \\to Σ^0\\barΣ^0η$. The signal significances, after considering systematic uncertainties, are determined to be 7.2$σ$, 5.7$σ$, and 6.7$σ$ for $χ_0$, $χ_{c1}$, and $χ_{c2}$, respectively. The branching fractions are measured to be $\\mathcal B(χ_{c0}\\toΣ^0\\barΣ^0η)=({9.7 \\pm 1.7 \\pm 0.8}) \\times 10^{-5}$, $\\mathcal B(χ_{c1}\\toΣ^0\\barΣ^0η)=({4.9 \\pm 1.1 \\pm 0.4}) \\times 10^{-5}$, and $\\mathcal B(χ_{c2}\\toΣ^0\\barΣ^0η)=({6.1 \\pm 1.2 \\pm 0.3}) \\times 10^{-5}$, where the first uncertainties are statistical and the second systematic. No significant structure in the $Σ^0\\barΣ^0,Σ^0η,\\barΣ^0η$ mass distributions is observed under the current statistics.",
